  "finalText": "The 12-second explainer is built in the **Main** composition (1920×1080, 30 fps), in three ~4 s beats that hand over without cuts. The critique scores it 97/100. Its one flag, a 0.7 s suction move on the last note, is intentional, so I left it.\n\n- **Messy notes (0–4 s):** Five flat sticky notes (pink, teal, yellow) pop in with a slight Back Out overshoot. They wobble anxiously on different rhythms while they sit in a pile.\n- **Suck into vault (3.5–4.7 s):** The notes accelerate into the centre, each one shrinking as it arrives (staggered by about 0.06 s). The navy shield pops in as the last note lands, then holds.\n- **Glow and headline (7.8–12 s):** A teal halo blooms behind the shield and pulses. A white check mark draws on inside the shield at 8.7 s, and \"One key. Every login.\" rises in at 8.3 s. The shield then breathes gently to the end.\n\nChoices I made:\n- The palette is cream background, navy ink, pink, teal and yellow.\n- The check mark sits inside the shield rather than beside the headline. If you want a second check next to the text, I can add one.\n- The shield is held still for about 3 s in beat 2, which gives the headline room to land.\n\nLayers are named (Sticky note 1–5, Vault shield, Shield glow, Headline). Next tweaks could be a bigger headline, a different accent colour for the glow, or a loop-friendly ending."
